He'd recorded his family history. Now, how about his community's history? He was under the impression at the time that the history of Central Louisiana was pretty well written. But still, he decided to take a look. And I remember reading in the Chamber of Commerce magazine, they had this did you know section. And one of the things in the did you know section was John Wesley Hardin, the West's greatest criminal, was housed in the Alexandria City jail. Well, what was he in jail for?
